But IMHO the game should make any changes on the level before saving the 
bones file, so that the bones loader don't have to know what had 
happened in the previous game.

The division of the work is very clear in the code. The bones saver 
makes changes that are pertinent to the game where the save happens 
before the save and loader makes changes to the loaded file that are 
pertinent to the game that loads the file.

For example here are few things the saver does:
- changes invocation items to mundane items.
- changes AoY to fake AoY.

These are few things that the loader handles:
- no duplicate artifacts.
- no genocided monsters.

